0,"Suri, Tirmaga-Chai | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/suq/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..yS0H1Gym5bptdkzLlaxC4weiRcOHipbi5TAUJchFR6A,Tirmaga-Chai Suri is a stable indigenous language of Ethiopia. It belongs to the Nilo-Saharan language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,"Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",Nilo-Saharan
1,Tirmaga-Chai Suri - suq (Nilo-Saharan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/suq/,"Tirmaga-Chai Suri (suq) is part of the Nilo-Saharan family and Nilo-Saharan, Satellite-Core, Core, Eastern Sudanic, Southern (n languages), Surmic, South, Southeast, Pastoral, Suri class. Tirmaga-Chai Suri speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts: Types.","Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",Nilo-Saharan
2,"ScriptSource - Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",https://scriptsource.org/cms/scripts/page.php?item_id=language_detail&key=suq&_sc=1,Alternate names. Tirmaga-Chai Suri. Dialects. Status.Is based on script. Tirmaga-Chai Suri written with Ethiopic script. suq-Ethi.,"Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",Nilo-Saharan
3,Suri language,https://grokipedia.com/page/suri_language,"The Suri language (also known as Chai or Tirma), spoken by approximately 32,000 people (as of 2016) of the Suri ethnic group in southwestern Ethiopia near the border with South Sudan, is a Southeastern Surmic language within the Nilo-Saharan phylum.","Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",Nilo-Saharan
4,"Suri, Tirmaga-Chai in Ethiopia people group profile | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/15130/ET,"Learn about the Suri, Tirmaga-Chai in Ethiopia people group. Profiles include statistics, text, photo, map, progress indicator and language resources.","Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",Nilo-Saharan
5,(PDF) Nilo-Saharan Languages,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/304040925_Nilo-Saharan_Languages,"Nilo-Saharan is essentially Greenberg's earlier Macro-Sudanic (or Chari-Nile) family, together with languages and language groups formerly assigned to historically isolated units.","Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",Nilo-Saharan
6,Suri Subordinate Clauses,https://www.diu.edu/documents/theses/Smith_Meaghan-thesis.pdf,The Chai and Tirmaga dialects of the Chai-Tirmaga-Mursi cluster correspond to the ISO 639-3 code [suq]. Suri is a member of the Surmic group within the Eastern Sudanic branch of the Nilo-Saharan language family.,"Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",Nilo-Saharan
7,Suri,https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Suri,"Language family: Nilo-Saharan, Eastern Sudanic, Eastern, Surmic, South, Southeast, Pastoral, Suri (SIL classification). Number of speakers: ~28,000.‘Suri’ is an ethnonym for speakers of the Tirmaga, Chai and Baale (see Kacipo-Balesi) speech varieties.","Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",Nilo-Saharan
8,Information to users,"https://theswissbay.ch/pdf/Books/Linguistics/Mega+linguistics+pack/African/Nilo-Saharan/Tirmaga+Grammar,+Aspects+of+(Bryant).pdf","Nilo-Saharan languages are known for their complexity in this area. Although no final conclusions have been made, some interesting semantic categories for marking number in Tirmaga have been observed.","Suri, Tirmaga-Chai",Nilo-Saharan
